div.p:
2. The Allied Authorities reserve the right:
(a) to take such measures as may be necessary for the maintenance of security, [the preservation of democratic government], the fulfillment of the international obligations and interests of their Governments, or the preservation of the economic and financial stability of Berlin;
(b) to act and legislate for the protection, prestige and security of the Allied forces, their dependents, employees and representatives, their immunities satisfaction of occ costs, and their other requirements.
